MJPEG fixtures of the host tests (tests/mjpeg_stream.hpp loads them; the streams
themselves are assembled in the test code from these pieces).

tiny_16x16.jpg, tiny_32x16.jpg -- baseline 4:2:0 JPEGs, made once with:
    ffmpeg -f lavfi -i testsrc=size=16x16:rate=1 -frames:v 1 -q:v 8 -pix_fmt yuvj420p -bitexact tiny_16x16.jpg
    ffmpeg -f lavfi -i testsrc=size=32x16:rate=1 -frames:v 1 -q:v 8 -pix_fmt yuvj420p -bitexact tiny_32x16.jpg

ipwebcam_head.bin -- the response head of an IP Webcam phone (IP Webcam Server 0.4)
    and the first part header, the JPEG body cut off: the bytes up to the end of the
    first part header, received after the GET that NetMjpegSource::send_get sends.
    Recorded 2026-11-14 for issue #28.

ref_evening_raw.csv -- layer B of the reference detections (issue #32, reference/README.md):
    the "raw" lines of reference/ref_evening.csv for two stretches of the clip, frames
    440..566 (a person walks out, dies into a ghost, the trail ages out; a new person
    spawns at 566) and 700..800 (empty, then a new entry). The cut right after the
    spawn at 566 is where test_reference_chain.cpp puts its 1.2 s stall: the tentative
    track dies by time -- the clip alone never kills one. Made with:
    awk -F, '/^[0-9]/{f=$1} ((f>=440 && f<=566) || (f>=700 && f<=800)) && !/^sm,/' \
        reference/ref_evening.csv > tests/data/ref_evening_raw.csv

ref_evening_golden.txt -- the output of test_reference_chain.cpp: the clip segment on that
    fixture, then two synthetic segments generated in the test code ("crossing": two
    persons walk through each other, one occluded for 3 frames; "weak": a merged blob
    only round 2 of the association accepts). Smoothed boxes, track states, GpuBoxes
    per frame; an "h <segment>" line opens each segment. Written on the board by the
    tracker / smoother / box mapper code of fix/audit-p0 @ f3c5a7f (unchanged in #33):
    first with the clip segment only, then regenerated once when the synthetic segments
    and the conf column (6 decimals) were added (review of #33); the clip segment
    stayed the same. Regenerate with:
    cmake -S tests -B build/tests && cmake --build build/tests --target light_ai_tests
    cd build/tests && LIGHT_AI_WRITE_GOLDEN=1 ./light_ai_tests
    Rewrite it only for a deliberate behavior change of BoxSmoother, Tracker or the
    box mapper -- never in a refactoring (re-baselined in Stage 4 for `BoxSmoother` skipping `cls == 0`, `Tracker` `kMaxMiss=6` / `P2-9`, and `YoloDecoder` `stable_sort` NMS; re-baselined on `feat/callout-2x-box-stabilize` for `BoxSmoother` interval-envelope locking).
    Tolerances (test_reference_chain.cpp): 1e-2 px for positions / sizes, 1e-1 px/s
    for velocities, 1e-4 for confidences; ids, states, counts, classes, colors, alpha
    exact. Measured (2026-11-15): the same code built with -ffp-contract=off (no fused
    multiply-add, as on an x86 host; GCC 13.3 x86_64 gives the same) deviates by at
    most 1e-4 px and 4e-4 px/s. Each of these local edits fails the test: the Tracker
    kQAccel 2000 -> 2100 (11.4 px, 6.6 px/s), round 2 of Tracker::associate switched
    off (the "weak" scenario: the track dies, a new id spawns), greedy_iou_match
    worst-first (the "crossing" segment, 30.5 px, 62.7 px/s).
